NAME
     getpw - get name from uid

DESCRIPTION
     The bracketed qualifier of section 5 goes on a centred second line under
     the banner.

XREF(1)                    UNIX Programmer's Manual                     XREF(1)

NAME
     xref - what is a cross-reference and what only looks like one

DESCRIPTION
     See open(2) and the discussion in ls(1). A subsection letter is part of
     it, so fsck(1m) and stdio.3s and exp(3m) are references too, and a name
     may begin with an underscore: _exit(2).

     The name must start at a word boundary, so sprintf(3) is one reference and
     not two: the printf inside it does not match on its own.

     A reference must carry no markup, and these are therefore not references:
     open(2) is a bold run, ls(1) is an italic one, and `printf(3)' is a
     literal one.

     Nor is anything whose shape is wrong: open(9) has no such section, open
     (2) has a space in it, open(2 has no close, and 9open(2) does not begin
     with a letter.

SEE ALSO
     malloc(3), free(3), realloc(3), calloc(3)
